      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:07 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Scott E. Gant)",
      "case_id": "2019-18-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b360289d7a29611552fe106378a728e4d40dea0637f66643ae458b16570577c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b360289d7a29-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "While this case is about the FDCPA, it is also fundamentally about the relationship between this Court and Congress. That relationship has long been governed in part by two important presumptions relevant here: first, that Congress legislates against the backdrop of the common law and, second, that Congress legislates aware of this Court's decisions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Official",
      "case_id": "2019-18-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b360289d7a29611552fe106378a728e4d40dea0637f66643ae458b16570577c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b360289d7a29-0001-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We do know that the first service was attempted at an address and it falsely represented that the defendant -- the plaintiff was personally served. He was not. It also represented he was black, according to the affidavit of service. He's not. He's Caucasian. It represented he was 51 years old. He was in his late 30s at the time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2019-18-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b360289d7a29611552fe106378a728e4d40dea0637f66643ae458b16570577c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b360289d7a29-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DVORETZKY: I don't think that that is common law self-concealing fraud."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b360289d7a29611552fe106378a728e4d40dea0637f66643ae458b16570577c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b360289d7a29-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Can I make sure --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2019-18-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b360289d7a29611552fe106378a728e4d40dea0637f66643ae458b16570577c4",
